<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Antanosy Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1825 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of the Anosy region in south-east Madagascar, the first Malagasy state to confront a French colony on the island.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanosy">Antanosy</a> kingdom took shape around 1500 in the fertile Anosy region near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taolagnaro">Taolagnaro</a>, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zafiraminia">Zafiraminia</a>, a ruling clan claiming descent from Muslim immigrants. They kept Arabic-script writing and certain Islamic customs while ruling a largely Malagasy population.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zafiraminia">Zafiraminia</a> nobles held ritual privileges, including the exclusive right to slaughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, and ruled over clans of commoners and slaves. The French governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etienne-de-flacourt">Etienne de Flacourt</a> described <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanosy">Antanosy</a> society in detail in his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/history-of-the-great-island-of-madagascar">History of the Great Island of Madagascar</a> of 1658. Relations with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fort-dauphin-colony">Fort-Dauphin Colony</a> swung between trade and war, with the French seizing cattle and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The French abandoned <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fort-dauphin-colony">Fort-Dauphin</a> in 1674 after an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanosy">Antanosy</a> uprising. The region remained divided among rival lords until the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/merina-kingdom">Merina Kingdom</a> conquered it in 1825. The Antanosy remain a distinct people of south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1825 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:6.47%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1825 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Malagasy religion with Islamic elements</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malagasy</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Anosy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1662&amp;focus=antanosy-kingdom" aria-label="Antanosy Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5945 2868 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Antanosy Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6286 3134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6265 3124h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6265 3124h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Madagascar. <a href="/atlas?year=1662&amp;focus=antanosy-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

